<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH COKOLADOVNY CZK 550.9 MLN 9MO NET.</title>
<headline>CZECH COKOLADOVNY CZK 550.9 MLN 9MO NET.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for nine-month period ending September 30, 1996, calculated according to Czech accounting standards: (in millions of crowns)  Net profit     550.918    vs    380.609</p>
<p> Gross profit   909.958    vs    677.144</p>
<p> Operating profit     1,004.626    vs     724.909</p>
<p> Production	     7,617.321    vs   6,356.154</p>
<p> Sales of goods	   168.640    vs     144.413</p>
<p>Sales of own products</p>
<p>  and services	  7,711.340    vs   6,356.154</p>
<p> Write-offs		 398.808    vs     283.662</p>
<p> Assets		   7,365.038    vs   6,553.842</p>
<p> Basic capital	  3,127.701    vs   3,127.701</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Cokoladovny a.s., one of the</p>
<p>Czech Republic's major confectioners. Its main shareholder --</p>
<p>which holds an 80 percent stake in the firm -- is Cokoladovny</p>
<p>Partners BV, a joint-venture between Danone and</p>
<p>Nestle SA .</p>
<p>-- Prague newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
